Status files read from a rooted LG C5 (kernel 5.4.268-329.ptl4tv.5) on
2026-11-11, with speakers as the output (no eARC receiver) and a Dolby MAT
source on HDMI port 0, decoder adec.p1. Copied verbatim; the test edits them
into each case's state. The number in a prop file's chain-profile line is
different on every read of the TV's file; it is not a setting.

hdmi, adec.p0, adec.p1, sndout   /proc/lgtv-driver/audio/<name>
hdmi1.prop, hdmi1.lstatus        /proc/aaudio/processors/dsp0/hdmi1/021c0001/{prop,lstatus}
gain.prop                        /proc/aaudio/processors/dsp2/gain/041b0001/prop
dot_module_connection            /proc/aaudio/dot_module_connection
dot_block_connection             /proc/aaudio/dot_block_connection
amixer-cget-numid92.txt          amixer -c0 cget numid=92

dot_block_connection lacks the compressed route (renderer_1_out100 ->
mixer_0_in100, mixer_0_out100 -> output_3_in0): this TV has no receiver. The
test's amixer stub appends those two lines, in the form lg-g5-dts's script
greps for; their exact text on a receiver TV has not been seen here.
